# <%= module.title %> CRUD Draft

Generated by `corepack pnpm generate:module` or the Web module generator.

This is a reviewable draft. Web-generated drafts stay offline in `generated/module-drafts` until you
publish them from `/system/module/generator`. Publishing applies the reviewed snippets and files into
the real project source.

## Target Files

| Piece | Target |
| --- | --- |
| Schema snippet | `<%= module.targetPaths.schema %>` |
| Migration snippet | `<%= module.targetPaths.migration %>` |
| Backend route | `<%= module.targetPaths.route %>` |
| Route registration snippet | `<%= module.targetPaths.systemRoute %>` |
| Feature page | `<%= module.targetPaths.feature %>` |
| App Router page | `<%= module.targetPaths.appPage %>` |
| Route manifest snippet | `<%= module.targetPaths.routeManifest %>` |
| Seed rule snippet | `<%= module.targetPaths.seedRule %>` |
| API test | `<%= module.targetPaths.test %>` |

## Apply Order

1. Paste `snippets/schema.entry.ts` into `<%= module.targetPaths.schema %>`.
2. Paste `snippets/migration.sql` into the next migration block in `<%= module.targetPaths.migration %>`.
3. Add `<%= module.table %>` to `triggerTables` when the table uses `updated_at`.
4. Copy `<%= module.targetPaths.route %>`, `<%= module.targetPaths.feature %>`, `<%= module.targetPaths.appPage %>`, and `<%= module.targetPaths.test %>` into the project.
5. Apply `snippets/system-route.entry.ts` to `<%= module.targetPaths.systemRoute %>`.
6. Apply `snippets/route-manifest.entry.ts` to `<%= module.targetPaths.routeManifest %>`.
7. Apply `snippets/seed-rule.entry.ts` to `<%= module.targetPaths.seedRule %>` and review the route ID.

## Module

- Table: `<%= module.table %>`
- Schema export: `<%= module.schemaName %>`
- API base path: `<%= module.apiPath %>`
- Frontend path: `<%= module.frontendPath %>`
- Permission prefix: `<%= module.permission %>`
- Parent rule: `<%= module.parentKey %>` (`<%= module.parentId %>`)

## Validate

```bash
corepack pnpm typecheck
corepack pnpm lint
corepack pnpm test -- <%= module.targetPaths.test %>
corepack pnpm admin:check-routes
```
